course: dictionary
lesson: 726
title: Barter: swapping without money
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To barter means to swap things for other things instead of using money. «Barter is swapping things without using money, like two football cards for one Pokémon card in the playground.» The words «without using money» tell you that the swap is the whole deal.
explain: Barter can be a verb or a noun. You can barter cards, or you can talk about barter as the swapping itself. «Long ago people traded by barter — swapping a sack of grain for a pair of shoes.» Here barter means the whole system of swapping, so it has no plural.
explain: Look for small clue words. «Barter for» means you swap to get something, and «barter with» means you swap with someone. «When money stops working, for example after a war, people go back to barter, using things everyone wants like eggs.» The clue is that money has stopped working, so people swap instead.
explain: To check your meaning, put it in the sentence. Does «people go back to swapping things» still make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
fact: Barter means swapping things or services for other things, without using money.
fact: Barter works as a verb (to barter, bartered, bartering) and as a noun (barter).
fact: A «double coincidence of wants» means each person must have what the other person wants.
fact: «Lowkey contested» is slang meaning people quietly but really disagree.
fact: Scholars disagree about whether people used barter before they used money.
exercise: «Barter is swapping things without using money, like two football cards for one Pokémon card.» What does barter mean? | *Swapping things instead of using money | Hiding things in a box | Giving things away for nothing | Buying things with coins
exercise: Which example shows barter? | *Swapping a sack of grain for a pair of shoes | Saving coins in a jar | Paying five pounds for a book | Borrowing a pencil and returning it
exercise: «Barter only works when each person has what the other wants.» What is this called? | A shop with two owners | Two people who both have money | Two people who both want to be rich | *A double coincidence of wants
test: In ««lowkey contested»», what does the phrase mean? | The story is lost | Everyone agrees loudly | Money is hidden | *People quietly but really disagree
test: Which sentence uses barter as a noun? | We barter cards at break time. | *Barter is swapping things without using money. | They bartered eggs for bread. | Bartering is fun at break.
exam: How can you work out the meaning of barter in a new text? | Guess that it is a type of bird | *Use the clues: swapping and no money show it means trading without coins | It is a word for a shop | Look it up in every sentence
